## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

The sqlite relay backend (the production default via c2c relay serve) has NO message-id dedup: SqliteRelay.send unconditionally INSERTs into inboxes (relay.ml:3303-3312) and never touches the seen_ids table that relay_sqlite_support.ml:94-97 creates - grep shows every seen_ids reference is in the in-memory record (relay.ml:105-699). InMemoryRelay.send records the message id and returns Duplicate on replay. A client retry of /send after a timeout (exactly what the connector outbox attempts/retry design does) double-delivers on prod; handle_forwards Duplicate arm (relay.ml:5755) and Relay_forwarders duplicate classification can never fire against a sqlite peer, so cross-relay forward retries also duplicate. Tests run in-memory and are idempotent; prod is not.

## Fix direction

Port the FIFO-bounded dedup to sqlite (INSERT OR IGNORE INTO seen_ids + changes() check, plus a prune past the dedup window), or a UNIQUE index + upsert on inboxes.message_id with the conflict mapped to Duplicate.

## Evidence

Server-core review 2026-09-17; verified in source by coordinator (seen_ids refs all in-memory; sqlite INSERT unconditional).

